### Iterative method
By setting `Method` to `"Iterative"`, we can estimate the material parameters more accurately by using almost all of the information available in the measured time traces. Let's compare the two methods.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
### Iterative method
By setting `Method` to `"Iterative"`, we can estimate the material parameters more accurately by using almost all of the information available in the measured time traces. Let's compare the two methods.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
unwrapped = UnwrapPhase[t, Method->"KKGuidedMultiscale"];
ListLinePlot[{
  EstimateMaterialParameter["\[Alpha]", unwrapped, Quantity[0.6, "Millimeters"], "Gain"->1.2],
  EstimateMaterialParameter["\[Alpha]", unwrapped, Quantity[0.6, "Millimeters"], Method->"Iterative", "Gain"->1.2]
}, PlotRange->{{0.2,4.0}, {-20,160}}, Frame->True, FrameLabel->{"f (THz)", "\[Alpha] (1/cm)"}, PlotLegends->{"-LogT / d", "Iterative solver for n and k"}]

