.md
## Circular basis (MCD, NCD, and others)
Our library can transform data acquired with linearly polarized light, using a special arrangement of polarizer and analyzer angles, to retrieve the circular components of the light. This is helpful when the eigenstates of light inside the probed medium are circularly polarized (as in Faraday rotation, MCD, and other effects). In this example, the data were measured at a fixed polarizer angle in two subsequent measurements with $\\text{Analyzer} = \\text{Polarizer}\\pm 45^\\circ$.

All transformations are performed in the time domain. Here is an example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Circular basis (MCD, NCD, and others)
Our library can transform data acquired with linearly polarized light, using a special arrangement of polarizer and analyzer angles, to retrieve the circular components of the light. This is helpful when the eigenstates of light inside the probed medium are circularly polarized (as in Faraday rotation, MCD, and other effects). In this example, the data were measured at a fixed polarizer angle in two subsequent measurements with $\\text{Analyzer} = \\text{Polarizer}\\pm 45^\\circ$.

All transformations are performed in the time domain. Here is an example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(* LOAD YOUR DATA *)
(* here we use example data stored in the notebook *)
{sam, ref} = NotebookRead[NotebookStore["contradictoriness-06c"]];


sam = QuantityArray[#, {"Picoseconds", 1}] &/@ sam;
ref = QuantityArray[#, {"Picoseconds", 1}] &/@ ref;

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
This effectively switches the basis from linear to circular:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
This effectively switches the basis from linear to circular:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
sam = LinearProjectionsToCircular[Sequence@@sam, {-45Degree, 45Degree}];
ref = LinearProjectionsToCircular[Sequence@@ref, {-45Degree, 45Degree}];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
`sam` and `ref` **can now be treated as usual**, including for material-parameter extraction and Fabry–Pérot deconvolution, **provided that the original data were measured using circularly polarized light**.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
`sam` and `ref` **can now be treated as usual**, including for material-parameter extraction and Fabry–Pérot deconvolution, **provided that the original data were measured using circularly polarized light**.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
t = MapThread[DeconvolveTraces[#1, #2]&, {sam, ref}];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
EstimateMaterialParameter["\[Alpha]", FrequencySpectrumTrim[#], Quantity[0.08, "Millimeters"]] &/@ t;
ListLinePlot[%, PlotRange->{{0.5,3.0}, {-150, 300}}, Frame->True, PlotStyle->{Red,Blue}, PlotLegends->{
  "CW", "CCW"
}]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(Legended[ToExpression[FrontEndRef["F7e5a2714-a0d1-42a9-b233-352ec93a458f"], InputForm], Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[PointSize[0.006944444444444445], AbsoluteThickness[2], RGBColor[1, 0, 0]], Directive[PointSize[0.006944444444444445], AbsoluteThickness[2], RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}, {"CW", "CCW"}, LegendMarkers -> {{False, Automatic}, {False, Automatic}}, Joined -> {True, True}, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> "Column"], After, Identity]])(*,*)(*"1:"*)(*]VB*)

