.md
The signal is strongly affected by FP fringes. However, we can attempt to remove them and compare the results.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
The signal is strongly affected by FP fringes. However, we can attempt to remove them and compare the results.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
unwrapped = UnwrapPhase[#, Method->"KKGuidedMultiscale"]&/@t;
With[{estimate = Function[fp, 
  ListLinePlot[
      MapThread[Select[
        ToStandardOpticsUnits[
          EstimateMaterialParameter["\[Alpha]", #, Quantity[0.08, "Millimeters"], 
            Method->{"Iterative", "SolveFP"->fp}, 
            "PhaseCorrection"->#2, "Gain"->0.6
          ]
        ], 
        Function[xy, xy[[1]]>=0.5 && xy[[1]]<=3.2]] &, 
      {unwrapped, {-4Pi,0}}], 
      FrameLabel->{"\[Omega] (THz)", "\[Alpha] (1/cm)"},
      PlotRange->{{0.5,3.0}, Automatic}, Frame->True, 
      PlotStyle->{Red,Blue}, PlotLegends->{"CW", "CCW"}]
]}, Row[{
  Labeled[estimate[True], "After", Top],
  Labeled[estimate[False], "Before", Top]
} // Reverse]] // Deploy 

